## Design decision (do this, don't deviate)

The screener index is a **single compact Parquet** (`signals/stocks/screener_index.parquet`), one row per ticker, scalar columns only. This mirrors `conviction_signals.parquet` / `alpha_signals.parquet`. Do NOT touch the conviction SQLite snapshots or its 5-layer cache — keep the screener fully standalone to avoid that complexity. (The large per-ticker deep-dive payloads remain one-file-per-ticker; only compact scalars go in this index.)

