## Acceptance criteria

- Nightly batch writes a single `signals/stocks/screener_index.parquet` (one row per ticker; scalar columns only). No per-ticker screener files; no monolithic deep-dive payloads in the index.
- Batch reads the v2 `DeepDiveStore` where present (no recompute), falls back to inline engine otherwise.
- `setup_score` / `setup_label` match the formulas above (unit-tested with crafted fixtures: a diamond scores ≥ 70 + "Prime Pullback"; an overbought-weak fixture is haircut + "Overextended").
- `GET /stocks/screener` filters/sorts correctly across all params and returns 200 + empty on a missing index.
- Frontend Screener page: `DataTable` with RSI/score range filters, Setup + Sector multiselect, Above-200-SMA boolean, preset recipe buttons, rows linking to Deep Dive; nav entry + `/stocks/screener` route.
- Screener works in GCS cloud mode via published JSON (no inline compute).
- `screener_index_batch_enabled=false` disables the batch cleanly.
- `cd backend && pytest tests/unit/` and `cd frontend && npm run build` both pass.

